I hope your modeſty / VVill knovv, vvhat diſtance to the Crovvn is due.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, obsolete","register":"countable, figuratively, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["action at a distance","aesthetic distance","angular distance","at a distance","automatic distance control","Bhattacharyya distance","biodistance","blockwise distance","braking distance","by some distance","cartesian distance","Cartesian distance","Chebyshev distance","chessboard distance","city block distance","creepage distance","critical distance","demidistance","distance clause","distance education","distance fog","distance formula","distance function","distance learner","distance learning","distanceless","distancelessness","distance line","distanceometer","distance teaching"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3a307ff347723ac73c","definition":"Often followed by from: to set (someone or something) at a distance (noun sense 1.1) from someone or something else.","example":"If therefore the Interpoſition of Gloceſterſhire diſtanceth VVorceſterſhire from confining on the VVeſt-Saxons, the Animadvertor ought to have vented his diſpleaſure not on Me, but on Bede, and [Henry of] Huntington, vvhoſe vvords I exactly tranſlated.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["action at a distance","aesthetic distance","angular distance","at a distance","automatic distance control","Bhattacharyya distance","biodistance","blockwise distance","braking distance","by some distance","cartesian distance","Cartesian distance","Chebyshev distance","chessboard distance","city block distance","creepage distance","critical distance","demidistance","distance clause","distance education","distance fog","distance formula","distance fu